# MCP Tools: githubmcp

ALWAYS include `arguments` in CallMcpTool calls. NEVER send empty `{}`.

### get_repo_structure
Get the file/folder tree structure of a GitHub repository.

| Field | Type | Required | Default | Description |
|-------|------|----------|---------|-------------|
| `owner` | string | yes |  | Repository owner (user or organization). |
| `repo` | string | yes |  | Repository name. |
| `ref` | string \| null | no | `null` | Branch, tag, or commit SHA. Defaults to the repo's default branch. |
| `max_depth` | integer \| null | no | `null` | Maximum depth of tree to display (e.g. 2 for top-level + one level). |
| `path_filter` | string \| null | no | `null` | Optional glob pattern to filter paths (e.g. "src/**"). |

Example:
CallMcpTool({ server: "githubmcp", toolName: "get_repo_structure", arguments: {"owner": "lqdflying", "repo": "chathub"} })

### get_workflow_run_logs
Get the logs for a GitHub Actions workflow run, highlighting failed steps.

| Field | Type | Required | Default | Description |
|-------|------|----------|---------|-------------|
| `owner` | string | yes |  | Repository owner (user or organization). |
| `repo` | string | yes |  | Repository name. |
| `run_id` | integer | yes |  | The numeric workflow run ID (from list_workflow_runs). |
| `max_chars` | integer | no | `20000` | Maximum log characters to return (default: 20000).<br>       Increase if you need more context, but be aware of response size. |

Example:
CallMcpTool({ server: "githubmcp", toolName: "get_workflow_run_logs", arguments: {"owner": "lqdflying", "repo": "chathub", "run_id": 5} })

### list_branches
List all branches in a GitHub repository.

| Field | Type | Required | Default | Description |
|-------|------|----------|---------|-------------|
| `owner` | string | yes |  | Repository owner (user or organization). |
| `repo` | string | yes |  | Repository name. |

Example:
CallMcpTool({ server: "githubmcp", toolName: "list_branches", arguments: {"owner": "lqdflying", "repo": "chathub"} })

### list_directory
List contents of a directory in a GitHub repository.

| Field | Type | Required | Default | Description |
|-------|------|----------|---------|-------------|
| `owner` | string | yes |  | Repository owner (user or organization). |
| `repo` | string | yes |  | Repository name. |
| `path` | string | no | `""` | Directory path within the repository. Use "" for root. |
| `ref` | string \| null | no | `null` | Branch, tag, or commit SHA. Defaults to the repo's default branch. |

Example:
CallMcpTool({ server: "githubmcp", toolName: "list_directory", arguments: {"owner": "lqdflying", "repo": "chathub"} })

### list_pull_requests
List pull requests in a GitHub repository.

| Field | Type | Required | Default | Description |
|-------|------|----------|---------|-------------|
| `owner` | string | yes |  | Repository owner (user or organization). |
| `repo` | string | yes |  | Repository name. |
| `state` | string | no | `"open"` | Filter by state: "open" (default), "closed", or "all". |
| `head` | string \| null | no | `null` | Filter by head branch (e.g. "feature/my-feature" or "myorg:feature/my-feature"). |
| `base` | string \| null | no | `null` | Filter by base branch (e.g. "main"). |
| `limit` | integer | no | `20` | Maximum number of PRs to return (default: 20). |

Example:
CallMcpTool({ server: "githubmcp", toolName: "list_pull_requests", arguments: {"owner": "lqdflying", "repo": "chathub"} })

### list_workflow_runs
List recent CI/CD workflow runs for a repository.

| Field | Type | Required | Default | Description |
|-------|------|----------|---------|-------------|
| `owner` | string | yes |  | Repository owner (user or organization). |
| `repo` | string | yes |  | Repository name. |
| `workflow_id` | string \| null | no | `null` | Optional workflow filename (e.g. "ci.yml") or numeric ID to filter by. |
| `branch` | string \| null | no | `null` | Optional branch name to filter runs by. |
| `status` | string \| null | no | `null` | Optional status filter: "queued", "in_progress", "completed",<br>    "action_required", "cancelled", "failure", "neutral", "skipped",<br>    "stale", "success", "timed_out", "waiting". |
| `limit` | integer | no | `10` | Maximum number of runs to return (default: 10). |

Example:
CallMcpTool({ server: "githubmcp", toolName: "list_workflow_runs", arguments: {"owner": "lqdflying", "repo": "chathub"} })

### merge_pull_request
Merge a pull request.

| Field | Type | Required | Default | Description |
|-------|------|----------|---------|-------------|
| `owner` | string | yes |  | Repository owner (user or organization). |
| `repo` | string | yes |  | Repository name. |
| `pull_number` | integer | yes |  | The pull request number to merge. |
| `commit_title` | string \| null | no | `null` | Optional custom commit title for the merge commit. |
| `merge_method` | string | no | `"merge"` | Merge strategy: "merge" (default), "squash", or "rebase". |

Example:
CallMcpTool({ server: "githubmcp", toolName: "merge_pull_request", arguments: {"owner": "lqdflying", "repo": "chathub", "pull_number": 5} })

### push_files
Commit one or more files to a branch in a single atomic commit.

| Field | Type | Required | Default | Description |
|-------|------|----------|---------|-------------|
| `owner` | string | yes |  | Repository owner (user or organization). |
| `repo` | string | yes |  | Repository name. |
| `branch` | string | yes |  | Target branch to push to (must already exist; use create_branch first). |
| `files` | array<object> | yes |  | List of file objects, each with:<br>   - "path": file path in the repo (e.g. "src/main.py")<br>   - "content": full UTF-8 text content of the file |
| `message` | string | yes |  | Commit message. |

Example:
CallMcpTool({ server: "githubmcp", toolName: "push_files", arguments: {"owner": "lqdflying", "repo": "chathub", "branch": "main", "files": [{}], "message": "Content"} })

### read_file
Read file contents from a GitHub repository, optionally returning a specific line range.

| Field | Type | Required | Default | Description |
|-------|------|----------|---------|-------------|
| `owner` | string | yes |  | Repository owner (user or organization). |
| `repo` | string | yes |  | Repository name. |
| `path` | string | yes |  | File path within the repository (e.g. "src/main.py"). |
| `ref` | string \| null | no | `null` | Branch, tag, or commit SHA. Defaults to the repo's default branch. |
| `start_line` | integer \| null | no | `null` | First line to return (1-based, inclusive). Omit to start from beginning. |
| `end_line` | integer \| null | no | `null` | Last line to return (1-based, inclusive). Omit to read to end. |

Example:
CallMcpTool({ server: "githubmcp", toolName: "read_file", arguments: {"owner": "lqdflying", "repo": "chathub", "path": "README.md"} })

### search_code
Search for text or regex patterns across files in a GitHub repository.

| Field | Type | Required | Default | Description |
|-------|------|----------|---------|-------------|
| `owner` | string | yes |  | Repository owner (user or organization). |
| `repo` | string | yes |  | Repository name. |
| `query` | string | yes |  | Search string or regex pattern. |
| `is_regexp` | boolean | no | `false` | If True, treat query as a Python regex pattern. |
| `include_pattern` | string \| null | no | `null` | Optional glob pattern to limit search to matching files (e.g. "*.py"). |
| `ref` | string \| null | no | `null` | Branch, tag, or commit SHA. Defaults to the repo's default branch. |
| `max_results` | integer | no | `50` | Maximum number of matching lines to return (default: 50). |

Example:
CallMcpTool({ server: "githubmcp", toolName: "search_code", arguments: {"owner": "lqdflying", "repo": "chathub", "query": "search query"} })

### todo_update
Update the status of a single todo item by its 0-based index.

| Field | Type | Required | Default | Description |
|-------|------|----------|---------|-------------|
| `index` | integer | yes |  | 0-based position of the task in the list. |
| `status` | string | yes |  | New status - "pending", "in_progress", or "completed". |

Example:
CallMcpTool({ server: "githubmcp", toolName: "todo_update", arguments: {"index": 5, "status": "value"} })

### todo_write
Update the in-session task list for tracking multi-step work.

| Field | Type | Required | Default | Description |
|-------|------|----------|---------|-------------|
| `todos` | array<object> | yes |  | List of task objects. Each must have:<br>   - "content": task description (str)<br>   - "status": "pending" \| "in_progress" \| "completed" |

Example:
CallMcpTool({ server: "githubmcp", toolName: "todo_write", arguments: {"todos": [{}]} })

### trigger_workflow
Trigger a workflow_dispatch event to run a CI/CD workflow.

| Field | Type | Required | Default | Description |
|-------|------|----------|---------|-------------|
| `owner` | string | yes |  | Repository owner (user or organization). |
| `repo` | string | yes |  | Repository name. |
| `workflow_id` | string | yes |  | Workflow filename (e.g. "ci.yml") or numeric ID. |
| `ref` | string | yes |  | Branch or tag name to run the workflow on (e.g. "main"). |
| `inputs` | object \| null | no | `null` | Optional key/value inputs defined in the workflow's workflow_dispatch config. |

Example:
CallMcpTool({ server: "githubmcp", toolName: "trigger_workflow", arguments: {"owner": "lqdflying", "repo": "chathub", "workflow_id": 5, "ref": "main"} })
